    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d703">

                <pb facs="1013" n="893" sameAs="frus:frus1922v01/pg893"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.77/2498: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Warren</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-04-10T12:00:00+09:00"><hi rendition="#italic">April 10,
                                1922—noon</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received April 10—5:47
                    a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>62. Your 32, April 8, 6 p.m. Matsudaira<anchor n="68" xml:id="d703-f1"/> called
                    upon his return; spoke of this matter and said that after considering with
                        Uchida<anchor n="69" xml:id="d703-f2"/> he desired to take the matter up
                    with me. Have since expressed to Uchida and Matsudaira my willingness to take
                    the matter up whenever they are ready but Uchida has been occupied with the Diet
                    and now is occupied with Privy Council so they have sought no opportunity to
                    take question up.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Warren</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d703-f1" n="68" xml:id="d703-f1-content">
                <p>Tsuneo Matsudaira, Secretary General of the Japanese delegation at the Washington
                    Conference.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d703-f2" n="69" xml:id="d703-f2-content">
                <p>Count Yasuya Uchida, Japanese Minister of Foreign Affairs.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
